$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2. A microwavable vial was charged with
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (17.62 mg, 0.015 mmol),
pyrimidin-5-ylboronic acid (28.3 mg, 0.229 mmol) and
4-(2-amino-2'-bromo-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthene]-7'-yl)-2-methylbut-3-yn-2-ol
(9) (63.0 mg, 0.152 mmol) in DME (1 mL) followed by addition of sodium
carbonate (2M solution) (0.23 mL, 0.457 mmol). The reaction mixture was
stirred at 80°C for 16 hrs. The reaction mixture was extracted with
EtOAc, organic layer was washed with brine and concentrated. The residue
was purified by FC on silica gel (10-80% DCM/MeOH/NH4OH in DCM).
4-(2-amino-2'-(pyrimidin-5-yl)-5H-spiro[oxazole-4,9'-xanthene]-7'-yl)-2-methylbut-3-yn-2-ol
(39 mg, 62.0 % yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, microwave vial used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Lead Optimization and Modulation of hERG Activity in a Series of
Aminooxazoline Xanthene β-Site Amyloid Precursor Protein Cleaving Enzyme
(BACE1) Inhibitors
