$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.2.2.
2,7-bis(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-9-decyl-carbazole
(5) A solution of dibromocarbazole 4 (2.20 g, 4.73 mmol),
bis(pinacolato)diboron (2.76 g, 10.87 mmol) and KOAc (2.65 g, 28.15 mmol)
in anhydrous dioxane (55 mL) was degassed for 30 min with a flow of
nitrogen. PdCl2(dppf) (690 mg, 0.85 mmol) was added and the mixture was
stirred at 80 °C overnight. The next day, the reaction mixture was cooled
to room temperature and quenched by addition of NH4Cl (50 mL). The
organic phase was separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3×75 mL). The organic phases were combined, dried (MgSO4) and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by column chromatography (gradient of
hexane/EtOAc, 92:8 to 88:12) afforded the diboronic ester 5 in 61% yield
as a foam which crystallized from EtOH as white crystals:
2,7-bis(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-9-decyl-carbazole
(5), yield 61%. m.p.: 117 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): 8.12 (d, J = 7.7
Hz, 2H), 7.89 (s, 2H), 7.68 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 2H), 4.38 (t, J = 7.4 Hz,
2H), 1.89 (m, 2H), 1.201.45 (m, 38H), 0.88 (m, 3H) ppm.13C NMR (CDCl3, 75
MHz): 140.6, 125.2, 125.0, 120.2, 115.4, 83.9, 43.04, 32.0, 29.71, 29.69,
29.6, 29.44, 29.36, 27.3, 25.1, 22.8, 14.3 ppm. IR (KBr): ν = 2995 (m),
2979 (m), 2926 (m), 2852 (w), 1626 (w), 1561 (w), 1485 (s), 1435 (m),
1390 (s), 1355 (s), 1341 (s), 1308 (s), 1266 (s), 1212 (m), 1146 (s),
1112 (m), 1074 (s), 999 (w), 980 (w), 965 (m), 877 (w), 858 (m), 815 (m)
cm-1. MALDI-TOF: 559 (100) [M+], 432 (12). C34H51B2NO4: Calcd for C
73.00, H 9.19, N 2.50; found: C 73.26, H 8.97, N 2.45.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective Dispersion of Single-Walled Carbon Nanotubes with Specific
Chiral Indices by Poly(N-decyl-2,7-carbazole)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lemasson, Fabien A.; Strunk, Timo; Gerstel, Peter; Hennrich, Frank;
Lebedkin, Sergei; Barner-Kowollik, Christopher; Wenzel, Wolfgang; Kappes,
Manfred M.; Mayor, Marcel
