$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl
7-(5-((4-(4-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)piperazin-1-yl)-phenoxy)methyl)-1,3-dimethyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-3-(3-(naphthalen-1-yloxy)propyl)-1H-indole-2-carboxylate
(26). A suspension of boronate ester 15 (0.752 g, 1.506 mmol), Cs2CO3
(1.26 g, 3.87 mmol), PdCl2(dppf) (0.205 g, 0.280 mmol), and bromide 25
(0.620 g, 1.332 mmol) in dry DMF (14 mL) was heated to 100 °C for 40 min
in a Biotage initiator 2 microwave reactor and then cooled to ambient
temperature. The mixture was poured into 250 mL of EtOAc, and the organic
layer was washed 3× with brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography (50-100%
EtOAc/hexanes). 0.604 g (60% yield) of the title compound. 1H NMR (300
MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ 10.52 (s, 1H), 8.21 (m, 1H), 7.86 (dd, J = 6.7, 2.6 Hz,
1H), 7.70 (dd, J = 7.4, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.53 (m, 2H), 7.45 (d, J = 8.2 Hz,
1H), 7.38 (m, 1H), 7.07 (m, 2H), 6.89 (m, 1H), 6.73 (m, 4H), 4.81 (br s,
2H), 4.25 (dt, J = 12.3, 6.6 Hz, 4H), 3.83 (s, 3H), 3.40 (m, 4H), 3.34
(m, 2H), 2.88 (m, 4H), 2.22 (m, 2H), 2.04 (s, 3H), 1.40 (s, 9H), 1.21 (t,
J = 6.7 Hz, 3H). MS (ESI) m/z = 758.4 (M + H+).
