$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-(6-(Azetidin-3-yl)-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-2-yl)pyrimidin-2-amine
(10). To a microwave vial was added tertbutyl
3-(2-chloro-4-morpholinothieno[3,2-d]pyrimidin-6-yl)azetidine-
1-carboxylate (60 mg, 1.0 mmol), 2-aminopyrimidine-5-boronic acid, and
pinacol ester (48 mg, 0.2 mmol) 1 M cesium carbonate solution in water
(0.44 mL, 0.44 mmol) followed by
1,1′-bis(diphenylphosphino)-ferrocenepalladium(II) chloride (20 mg, 0.03
mmol). The mixture was degassed under nitrogen for 5 min, then subjected
to microwave irradiation at 140 °C for 30 min. The crude mixture was
filtered through a thin layer of Celite, and the filtered organics were
diluted with EtOAc and washed with water. The organic layer was
concentrated under reduced pressure and partially purified by silica gel
chromatography. The partially purified intermediate (60 mg, 1.0 mol) was
treated with TFA (1 mL) in CH2Cl2 (1 mL), and stirred 1 h. Saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 was added, and the aqueous layer was extracted with 10%
MeOH/EtOAc, dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated to give 10 after
HPLC purification. Yield 31 mg, 59% (over two steps). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO) δ 9.18-9.02 (s, 2H), 7.63-7.45 (s, 1H), 7.18-6.96 (s, 2H),
4.44-4.30 (p, J= 8.0 Hz, 1H), 4.31-4.18 (t, J= 9.1 Hz, 2H), 4.11-4.00
(dd, J= 9.8, 7.4 Hz, 2H), 4.00-3.90 (t, J= 4.7 Hz, 4H), 3.85-3.72 (t, J=
4.7 Hz, 4H). LC/MS (ESI+): m/z 370.1 (M + H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (in stage 1), thermal (in stage 1), Suzuki coupling
in stage 1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Design and Identification of Brain Penetrant Inhibitors of
Phosphoinositide 3-Kinase α
