$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
9-Ethyl-6,6-dimethyl-8-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-11-oxo-6,11-dihydro-5H-benzo[b]carbazole-3-carbonitrile
(7). 1-Methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole
(34 mg, 0.16 mmol) and 37 (60 mg, 0.13 mmol) were dissolved in
1,4-dioxane (5 mL) and 2 M Na2CO3 satd aq solution (0.17 mL, 0.34 mmol)
and thoroughly degassed. Pd(dppf)Cl2 (6 mg, 0.008 mmol) and t-Bu-XPhos (4
mg, 0.005 mmol) were added, and the mixture was heated to 100 °C in a
sealed vial. After the mixture was stirred for 1 h, LC/MS analysis
indicated the reaction was finished. The reaction mixture was filtered
through Celite and purified by reversed-phase HPLC using a gradient of
30-100% CH3CN/H2O with 0.035% TFA.
9-Ethyl-6,6-dimethyl-11-oxo-8-(thiophene-2-yl)-6,11-dihydro-5H-benzo[b]carbazole-3-carbonitrile
(12). The procedure used to prepare compound 7 was used to prepare
compound 12. Purification by reversed-phase HPLC using a gradient of
20-90% CH3CN/H2O with 0.035% TFA gave the desired compound as a beige
solid (31 mg, 58% yield). 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6, 400 MHz) δ 12.78 (s, 1H),
8.36 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 8.15 (s, 1H), 8.02 (s, 1H), 7.71 (m, 2H), 7.65
(m, 2H), 7.32 (d, J = 6 Hz, 1H), 2.81 (q, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 1.78 (s, 6H),
1.21 (t, J = 8 Hz, 3H); MS m/z 397.26 (M + 1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
