$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-(5-(Imidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-6-yl)pyridin-3-yl)benzenesulfonamide (3e). To
a solution of 6-bromoimidazo[1,2-a]pyridine (160 mg, 0.83 mmol) in
1,4-dioxane/water (3:1) (5 mL) were added
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridin-3-amine (180 mg,
0.83 mmol), K2CO3 (460 mg, 3.3 mmol), and PdCl2(dppf) •CH2Cl2 (34 mg,
0.041 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred at 100 °C for 12 h and
then cooled to rt. After removal of the solvent, the residue was purified
by flash column chromatography (MeOH:CH2Cl2, 1:20) to give the desired
product (33 mg, 19% yield). To a solution of above solid (20 mg, 0.10
mmol) and pyridine (12 μL, 0.14 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL) were added
benzenesulfonyl chloride (15 μL, 0.16 mmol). The resulting reaction
mixture was stirred at rt for 24 h and then concentrated in vacuo. The
residue was purified by flash column chromatography (MeOH:CH2Cl2, 1:20)
to give 3e as a white solid (10 mg, 30% yield).
N-(5-(1H-Pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin-5-yl)pyridin-3-yl)benzenesulfonamide (3d).
Compound 3d was prepared (56%), according to the procedure described for
3e. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6, 300 MHz) δ 6.54 (d, 1H, J = 1.98 Hz), 7.58 (m, 4H),
7.73 (m, 1H), 7.82 (s, 1H), 7.84 (s, 1H), 8.15 (s, 1H), 8.25 (m, 1H),
8.38 (s, 1H), 8.60 (s, 1H), 10.60 (br, 1H), 11.80 (s, 1H).
